// POST /queue/:entryId/claim
router.post("/queue/:entryId/claim", async (req, res) => {
  const { rows } = await db.query(
    `UPDATE queue_entries
        SET claimed_by = $1, claimed_at = now()
      WHERE id = $2 AND claimed_by IS NULL
      RETURNING id, student_id, claimed_by`,
    [req.user.id, req.params.entryId]
  );
  if (rows.length === 0) return res.status(409).json({ error: "already claimed" });
  io.to(req.params.courseId).emit("queue:claimed", rows[0]);
  res.json(rows[0]);
});
```

The `WHERE claimed_by IS NULL` makes Postgres decide the winner: the second TA's update matches 0 rows. On the client, handle 409 by refreshing the queue instead of showing an error.
